# AIPT - detection pack for LLM-driven autonomous pentest tools
# File:       aipt-block-eligible.sids - sids an operator MAY convert from alert to drop (inline IPS) after observation
# Version:    1.0.0 (2026-10-12)
# License:    Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
#
# Every rule of this pack ships with action alert. The sids below carry "metadata: policy block-eligible": a
# product-specific indicator (a tool's own User-Agent, console title, response body, cookie, JWT subject, LLM tool-set
# or marker) that produced 0 alerts on the 510,680-request synthetic benign corpus and on lab runs 04 (benign browsing)
# and 05 (ZAP baseline); see docs/fp-report.md. Generic and shape rules (policy alert / informational) are never
# listed here and must never be converted to drop.
#
# MANDATORY before converting any of them: run the pack in observe mode (alert only) on your own traffic over a period
# that contains normal peaks, batch windows, QA automation and at least one authorised assessment (DEPLOYMENT.md),
# review every alert of these sids, and convert only the sids with zero unexplained alerts. This list is a set of
# candidates for local policy review, not a recommendation to convert it wholesale. Convert per sensor
# position (a sid that is quiet on the perimeter may not be on an LLM gateway). The five ARTEX conversation-marker sids
# (9500032, 9500033, 9500034, 9500071, 9500072) may be converted on an egress proxy only, never on an LLM gateway or chat
# proxy sensor: a conversation about the tool (a user pasting its prompts or transcripts) reproduces the indicator. Keep
# the list under change control.
# A block-eligible sid whose enforcement is not yet validated by a fixture is listed as "# deferred gid:sid" and is
# not converted until that validation exists. Keep deferred entries commented out.
# Format: one "gid:sid" per line, preceded by a comment with file and message, so the file (or the lines you keep)
# can be used directly as a suricata-update drop.conf / modify list after the observation period.
#

